Exercise 2 — PID → Port
I performed the investigation in the opposite direction by starting with a known PID and checking whether it had an associated network connection.
Result:
PID: 2324
Process: svchost.exe
Port: 49666
 Key Lesson
I learned that Windows investigations can work in both directions:
PORT → PID → PROCESS → SERVICE → STATE
or:
PID → PORT
This is useful when investigating either a suspicious network port or a suspicious process.
 Day 3 Final Takeaway
A cybersecurity analyst can correlate network activity with running processes and Windows services to understand what is happening on a host.
